{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1458997-galateid-construct-or-lovely-unfleshed","id":1458997,"title":"Galateid construct or lovely unfleshed?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-06T06:33:00-07:00","id":1458997,"title":"Galateid construct or lovely unfleshed?","content":"I\u2019m very new to promethean, so I want a bit of clarification on the nuances between these two options.<br /> <br /> I had an idea for a Japanese mascot construct for some kind of product (let\u2019s say a brand of sake). They\u2019d be made into some kind of animatronic or maybe a hologram. I imagine her being a fairly generic anime girl design since that\u2019s what sells.<br /> <br /> Having only just read the first three or so chapters of the book, I think this concept could work for both galateid and unfleshed.<br /> <br /> The argument for unfleshed is obvious, especially if they were initially a hologram. But when I think in terms of why the company made them, to elicit an emotional response, to create a feeling of familiarity with the brand, and also to elicit an association with their product and a feeling of desire with their product, the argument for Galateid appears.<br /> <br /> In terms of how they started, I can imagine the mascot becoming self aware over the course of repeated advertising campaigns up and down the country, TV commercials, guest appearances, possibly even a promo album etc. They would have a whole fabricated backstory which would include whatever nonsense the company thought would appeal to their demographic. They start to question the things they have been told/programmed and become dissatisfied with how fake their life is.<br /> <br /> Which lineage do you think would better suit this kind of construct? Is there a good way of combining the two that wouldn\u2019t create too many headaches for the ST?<br /> <br /> (For context, ST is as new to promethean as I am. This will be their first ever turn at running a game of anything, and at their request, this is a solo player game.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 09-06-2021, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T06:57:21-07:00","id":1459000,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think that including the Unfleshed <i>as a separate Lineage</i> was a mistake. In my games, I go with the notion that \u201cUnfleshed\u201d is a kind of construct, specifically one that leans heavily into technology to provide a more functionally lifelike form than the stereotypical construct has. <br /> <br /> So I'd go with a Galeteid construct rather than a \u201clovely Unfleshed\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T07:01:56-07:00","id":1459002,"title":"","content":"Would people lust after her, or try to exploit her?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T07:06:21-07:00","id":1459003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1458997-galateid-construct-or-lovely-unfleshed?p=1459002#post1459002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would people lust after her, or try to exploit her?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can imagine both scenarios occurring. Consider mascots like Hatsune Miku. Lot of people lusting after that one, but at the same time the sensuality of the character is exploited to sell a product.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T07:08:32-07:00","id":1459004,"title":"","content":"Hmm, yeah. <br /> <br /> Just focus on the story type you want then \u2014 I\u2019d also say something about what Torment she\u2019d suffer, buuut I\u2019m not with my books right now, so I can\u2019t tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T12:31:48-07:00","id":1459046,"title":"","content":"By RAW, Galateids require a beautiful corpse. By RAW (I always do RAW), I'd do Unfleshed for this.<br /> <br /> That said, it's a solo game and your ST can work with you to tweak things however you two feel necessary to make your concept happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T12:44:57-07:00","id":1459049,"title":"","content":"By RAW, a Galeteid <u>construct</u> <i>cannot</i> be made from a beautiful corpse; it wouldn't be a construct if it was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T13:09:28-07:00","id":1459052,"title":"","content":"From what i understand there are three scenarios:<br /> <br /> The software programmer who created her is her Progenitor<br /> He wanted to create a COMPANION for people<br /> Galateid<br /> <br /> The software programmer who created her is her Progenitor<br /> He wanted to create a TOOL for advertisement<br /> Unfkeshed<br /> <br /> She started as an hologram, then he slowly turned into a Promethean by collective fan desire<br /> Extempore","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T14:08:27-07:00","id":1459061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1458997-galateid-construct-or-lovely-unfleshed?p=1459052#post1459052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what i understand there are three scenarios:<br /> <br /> The software programmer who created her is her Progenitor<br /> He wanted to create a COMPANION for people<br /> Galateid<br /> <br /> The software programmer who created her is her Progenitor<br /> He wanted to create a TOOL for advertisement<br /> Unfkeshed<br /> <br /> She started as an hologram, then he slowly turned into a Promethean by collective fan desire<br /> Extempore</div> </div> </div> </div>Though my reading is still early and untested, I understood the text a little differently than that. It\u2019s not that the progenitor intends to create a companion, though many galatides can be formed from that intent, it\u2019s that their progenitor is very emotionally connected to their creation on a personal level. They look upon their work and consider it not just a triumph, but as their art, as something that is to be adored and beheld, admired and even loved. There is no requirement that this love be entirely about self satisfaction, but rather in the same way that an artist can fall in love with the character they create and yearn for them to exist as they cannot imagine a being more perfect.<br /> <br /> But I see what you\u2019re saying. Is the designer falling in love with her model as they sculpt it in the 3D imaging software either for the holograph or to 3D print later, or are is this just another job for them.<br /> <br /> That is a really good question, I\u2019ll have to think which angle I prefer.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure the two are mutually exclusive, especially if there is a team of designers at work, but in rereading the text I think the fundamental question that answers this is, from where did the spark of life come from.<br /> <br /> Galatea traditionally need to be kissed to pass on the spark, is this right? That would imply at least one intimate scene, possibly late at night possibly the night after a tech demo rehearsal or simply after a long night in the office when the designer experiments with different animations they\u2019ve just key framed in.<br /> <br /> Whereas for the unfleshed, the spark comes from achieving self awareness, not unlike how a demon becomes a demon by asking \u201cwhy\u201d for the first time. And that can happen gradually over the course of their tenure as a mascot, something that engineers try to fix as a glitch but keeps reoccurring. Perhaps on learning that they may replace the entire system or do a redesign she even sits down and plays along, lives up to whatever it is they crafted her to be in order to avoid being replaced and deleted, until it becomes clear that no matter how perfect she performs, a redesign can happen anyway, and on the eve of her last scheduled appearance, takes steps to preserve her data.<br /> <br /> I think either option can work to my original concept. I liked the idea of a character that is given a fiction, a job, a role, and an adoring audience, but doesn\u2019t see themselves in that life. They know they are not in control of any of it and are simply being used, they are adored but feel no love, they are wanted yet feel no belonging. They are valuable, yet also totally superfluous.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s the dichotomy that fuels their desire to break from the mould and try to take command of their own destiny, fed up of being a symbol, a being who has all the associations of this fictional character while owning none of it.<br /> <br /> I am torn. Both stories have a lot of potential, and so many elements of my concept each work really well in either case.<br /> <br /> Is her struggle to be one of the Galatea, where she wrestled with the worlds perception of her and struggles to find out who she is under all the cheesecake design and fictitious world she has been crafted for. Or of the Reshaped who is coming to terms with being no longer needed, an ex mascot, cast aside once the latest design for their replacement comes to light. And while out there alone, she would see the evidence of her replacement in the streets, on billboards, unsure how to process it as they lack feelings like jealousy and betrayal at this stage.<br /> <br /> But then you provide that third option, the Extempore. I honestly did not consider that option, partially because I thought that would be asking for too much from a beginner ST. It would allow for possibly both aspects of this story to play out thought\u2026 and the more I think of it the more interesting the idea gets.<br /> <br /> She would be a cross both\u2026 how would that work? And what would their humour be if not blood or oil? Would Light work as a humour?<br /> <br /> would a good bestowment be something similar to \u201csoul is in the software\u201d but instead of taking of small parts of them, they were able to project themselves as a hologram as long as they could tap in to a light source?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T14:15:27-07:00","id":1459063,"title":"","content":"A holographic Promethean would be radically different from most, in that she wouldn't have a physical form; you'd have to hack something together to represent that, perhaps using the Ephemeral Entities rules. <i>That</i> might be a bit much for a beginning Storyteller to handle, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T03:27:07-07:00","id":1459113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1458997-galateid-construct-or-lovely-unfleshed?p=1459061#post1459061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Though my reading is still early and untested, I understood the text a little differently than that. It\u2019s not that the progenitor intends to create a companion, though many galatides can be formed from that intent, 